---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="What Xematics stores, what it never sends, and how analytics consent works."
>
  <article class="page prose">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy and cookies</p>
    <h1>Your diagrams stay with you.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Xematics has no accounts and no servers that store your work. The site is a set of static
      files served by GitHub Pages; everything the editor does happens in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your workspace.</strong> Diagrams and editor settings are saved in your browser's
        storage (IndexedDB) so they are there when you come back. They never leave your device
        unless you save a workspace file or share a link. Clearing this site's data in your browser
        removes them, so save the workspace if you want a copy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Two small preferences</strong> in local storage: your light or dark theme choice and
        your answer to the analytics question.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Share links</h2>
    <p>
      A share link carries the diagram in the part after the <code>#</code>. Browsers never send
      that part to any server, including GitHub and Google, so the diagram travels only to the
      people you give the link to.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics, only with your consent</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept, we use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are used. It sets
      cookies named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>. If you decline, or do not answer,
      Google Analytics is not loaded at all and no cookie is set.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google receives the page address without the <code>#</code> part, so it never sees your
      diagrams. We do not send diagram contents, file names or editor actions. Google processes the
      data under its own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Declining later stops analytics and removes its cookies. You can change your answer at any
      time with the button below or the Cookie settings link in the footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-consent-open>
        Open cookie settings
      </button>
    </p>

    <h2>Fonts and other requests</h2>
    <p>
      All fonts and code are served from this site itself. The editor does not contact any other
      service.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Ask on the project's <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/issues`}>GitHub issues</a> page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 46rem;
    padding-block: 48px 24px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 36px 0 8px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  p,
  li {
    max-width: 40em;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
